title: 'Dennis, Shabahang, Guo and Patil (2026): three rounds of compaction kept about 37% of what ten software conversations had established; corrections of procedure and facts of the project were lost most.'
pid: 863acb80-d2a0-46b6-a30e-dec25e0413bf
body: |2-
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.24657
  Abstract. Their point is weight training (80% kept), which we cannot
  do. Took: summarizing a summary loses most of what was particular,
  and "Jeff corrected this" is the kind of fact lost first.
